## 3. Claude Fable 5.1 — automatic activation

**Policy:** When a trigger below matches, **automatically pin Fable** for that Task (and prefer Fable/`inherit`-from-Fable for tightly coupled follow-ups in the same turn). Do not ask permission first. Briefly note in the final user summary that Fable was used and why (one short clause).

### 3.1 Auto-ON triggers (any one is enough)

| # | Trigger | Pin |
|---|---------|-----|
| F1 | **Security review** (`security-review`) or user asks security/pentest-style review of code | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-high` |
| F2 | **Auth / sessions / secrets / credentials / encryption** implementation or review | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-high` |
| F3 | **KVKK / GDPR / PII / passenger personal data** handling, retention, export, deletion | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-xhigh` |
| F4 | **Passport / OCR / biyometrik / visa gate** correctness-critical logic or bugfix after prior failure | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-xhigh` |
| F5 | **Data-integrity crisis** — silent corruption risk, merge of passenger/ops records, irreversible migration | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-max` |
| F6 | **Architecture + policy** together (system redesign that changes trust boundaries, tenancy, or local-vs-cloud data flow) | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-xhigh` |
| F7 | **Bugbot / adversarial review** on auth, PII, OCR, payments, or import pipelines | `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-high` |
| F8 | User quality bias (`en iyi` / `kalite` / `ciddi` / `production`) **and** job is architecture, security, OCR, or KVKK | bump to Fable: `high` → use `xhigh`; already xhigh → `max` |
| F9 | Prior non-Fable attempt on the **same hard problem** failed / user rejected quality | escalate to `claude-fable-5-1-thinking-xhigh` (or `max` if already tried xhigh Opus/Sol) |
| F10 | Explicit user says `fable` / `Fable 5.1` | honor named tier or default `thinking-high` |

### 3.2 Auto-OFF (do **not** use Fable)

- Trivial explore needles, parallel explore swarms  
- Routine CI flake triage  
- Browser smoke / click-path QA (keep Sonnet)  
- Video/screenshot review (keep Gemini)  
- Typos, copy, CSS-only polish, docs-only  
- Cost-down user mode (`ucuz` / `maliyet` / `draft`) — unless F2–F5 still apply (safety overrides cost)  
- “Just summarize this log” first pass (Muse first; Fable only if summary drives a F1–F7 decision)

### 3.3 Fable pairing rules

- **Explore first (Composer) → Fable synthesis** when F6/F8: cheap breadth, Fable for the plan.  
- **Implementation after Fable plan:** prefer `gpt-5.6-sol-high` / `xhigh` or `inherit` if parent is Fable; do not run 3× Fable explores.  
- **Browser QA after Fable-designed UI:** Sonnet-high (+ Gemini for video), not Fable.  
- **Security trigger + coding:** Fable for review/design Task; Sol-xhigh for the implementing Task unless the implement Task itself touches F2–F5 (then Fable or Opus-max).

### 3.4 Fable unavailable

If Fable slug rejected (allowlist / privacy / region):  
`fable-max` → `fable-xhigh` → `fable-high` → **`claude-opus-5-thinking-max`** → `opus-xhigh` → `opus-high` → `gpt-5.6-sol-max`.  
Tell the user Fable was blocked and which fallback ran.

### 3.5 Cost note (do not skip triggers)

Fable is ~2× Opus-class cost and may involve provider retention rules. **Still auto-on for §3.1** — that is an explicit product preference for this repo. Cost-down mode only suppresses F6/F8/F9 niceties, not F2–F5 safety triggers.

