## 7. Quality / cost bias

| Signal | Effect |
|--------|--------|
| `en iyi` / `kalite` / `ciddi` / `production` / `merge` | +1 effort tier; ban `-fast`; enable F8 (Fable on arch/security/OCR/KVKK) |
| `fable` named | Force §3.1 F10 |
| `hızlı` / `ucuz` / `maliyet` / `draft` | Allow Composer-fast, Terra, medium; **keep F2–F5 Fable auto-on** |
| Named other model | That model for turn + children unless unsafe vs F2–F5 (then Fable still for the sensitive Task) |
| Silence | §5 primaries at **high**; Fable still auto on §3.1 |

---

## 8. Anti-patterns

- Skipping Fable when §3.1 matches because it is “expensive” or “user didn’t say Fable”.  
- Leaving Task `model` unset.  
- Fable (or Opus) explore swarms — Composer for breadth.  
- Fable for browser smoke or video review.  
- Gemini/Muse as backend implementers.  
- `composer-2.5-fast` on OCR, auth, KVKK, UI redesign, migrations.  
- Downgrading because old Auto habit used Sonnet/Composer.  
- Using Fable-low/medium for §3 triggers — minimum **high**.

---

## 9. Launch checklist

1. Run §3 Fable triggers → if hit, pin Fable tier.  
2. Else §5 job row primary.  
3. Apply §7 bias.  
4. Pass `model` explicitly.  
5. On rejection → §6; report Fable block if relevant.  
6. In user-facing summary, if Fable auto-ran: one clause (“Fable 5.1 used for KVKK/auth review”).
